# NOTE: gitignore has no inline-comment syntax — a trailing "# ..." on a pattern
# line is taken as literal glob text and matches nothing.  Comments go on their
# own line.

# --- Copyrighted / captured material: kept LOCAL only, never committed -------
# The Macintosh release, in every shape it passes through on the way to being
# disassembled.  Same policy as the Rescue on Fractalus (.xex) and Revs (.ssd)
# repos: the game binary is not ours to distribute, and neither is anything
# derived from it byte for byte.
#
# ⚠ A Mac application arrives in MORE shapes than a single ROM/disc image did, and
# each one is a separate way to commit it by accident:
*.sit
*.sitx
*.hqx
*.bin
*.macbin
*.as
*.dsk
*.img
*.dmg
*.toast
*.iso
# AppleDouble sidecars — how a resource fork survives on a non-HFS filesystem.
# ⚠⚠ THIS IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS: `._Vette` IS the executable code.  A resource
# fork extracted this way looks like macOS noise and is the actual game.
._*
.AppleDouble/
# macOS puts a resource fork here on some filesystems too.
*/rsrc
# --- ...and everything derived from it ---------------------------------------
# disasm/ is generated by tools/ (resource + segment extraction) or a headless
# Ghidra pass.  Ignoring the directory rather than each output means a new dump
# does not need a new rule here.  The CURATED files are named back in.
disasm/*
!disasm/symbols.csv
# Screenshots, framebuffer captures and comparison images — of the original and
# of the port.  This also covers docs/*.png, so a documentation image has to live
# outside the repo too.
*.png
*.ppm
*.pgm
# Amiga Kickstart / Mac ROM images.  These land at the repo root as easily as a
# savestate does.
*.rom

# --- Build output ------------------------------------------------------------
build/
amiga/obj/
amiga/out/
amiga/.run/
*.o
*.d
*.elf
*.exe
*.map

# --- Ghidra install + annotation project (never commit) ----------------------
# tools/ghidra has NO trailing slash: it is a SYMLINK to a shared install
# (~/.local/share/ghidra, also used by the Rescue on Fractalus and Revs repos),
# and a trailing-slash pattern only matches a real directory, not a symlink to one.
tools/ghidra
tools/ghidra-proj/
tools/__pycache__/

# --- Local scratch -----------------------------------------------------------
# tmp/ is LOCAL ONLY, always (user instruction).  It is where the source archive,
# emulator captures, savestates and ad-hoc probe scripts live.  The loose patterns
# below are deliberate: a fresh savestate or dump normally lands at the repo root,
# not tidily inside tmp/.
/tmp/
*.dat
*.uss
*.sav
tools/live_*.sh
amiga/*_probe.sh

# --- OS / local tooling state ------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.claude/*.lock
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
# FS-UAE writes a .uaem metadata sidecar next to every file in a directory it
# mounts as an Amiga hard drive (run.sh mounts .run/dh0 + dh1), so this is a
# global guard.
*.uaem

# --- MAME's own state, written into the CWD ----------------------------------
# MAME writes cfg/ and nvram/ relative to the working directory unless told
# otherwise, so a bare run drops emulator state in the repo root -- and it WAS
# committed once before this rule existed.  The reference invocation now passes
# -cfg_directory / -nvram_directory into ref/mame/; these two entries are the
# backstop for a run that forgets.
/cfg/
/nvram/

# --- Reference-emulator material (never commit) ------------------------------
# ref/ holds the Macintosh reference loop's local-only inputs and state: ROM
# images, System / game disk images, MAME cfg+nvram, savestates and captures.
# None of it is ours to distribute.  Broad on purpose — *.rom alone would not
# cover a .zip romset, a device ROM named *.bin, or a boot image.
/ref/
